WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.067
-That's got to feel good, bud.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.267
I always love seeing you here.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.901
Thanks for coming back.
-I love being here.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.167
It's great to be back.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:10.133
-I got -- When I said hi to you,
I got mustache envy.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:14.133
Immediately, I go,
"That is a real stache."

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.834
Look at that thing.
-It is real.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.067
-Yeah. I was going to say.
Yeah. Wow.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.300
I mean, is it --
-New 'tache new job, you know?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.501
-Oh, yeah.
So, this is for a movie, yeah.

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:21.901
-It's for a movie.
-Oh.

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:26.167
-Playing a cop in the '80s
in a film called "The Order,"

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.634
which I start
in a couple of weeks.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.968
-Do you like that better
than a fake mustache?

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.334
-Yeah, for sure.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:36.167
I wore a fake, like,
beard or mustache maybe once.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.200
It was, like -- You know,
it's like acting through a rug,

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.534
and you can't smile,
particularly.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:46.200
So, yeah, I like growing the --

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.434
-"Police. Don't move.
Freeze! Freeze!"

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.634
-And the smiles,
because you get the "ping!"

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.467
-Ping! It pops up.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:56.067
-I recently -- Because
I just want to show you

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.934
how hard it is
for me to grow a mustache.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.968
This is my
senior yearbook photo.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:03.901
And it's -- Can you see it?
Can you zoom in?

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.367
That's a real --

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:12.400
That's that age where
that takes months.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.367
-That was commitment.
-You're like...[ Grunts ]

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:15.701
-Yeah. And if the wind blows,

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:16.968
it just kind of
blows in the wind.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:20.167
It was a very wispy,
free mustache.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.601
I wanted to
-I unscrew this every night.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.300
-No, that's a fantastic one.
That is a solid.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.467
I want to ask you about this,

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.234
because the Internet's
all abuzz.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.434
You just wrapped
"Star Wars: Skeleton Crew."

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.200
And there's a lot of buzz
going around it

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.434
and not a ton of information
about what it's about.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:37.767
And this is all I know so far.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.801
"Jude Law is in
'Star Wars: Skeleton Crew,'

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:45.100
an unnamed Jedi assisting
four children on an adventure."

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:51.834
That's vague.
-That's one perspective.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.701
-Wow. I'm intrigued.

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:57.100
-That sounds good.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.167
-You're not really allowed
to talk much?

00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.300
-Not much.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.934
There are wonderful,
as you can imagine,

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.968
twists and turns
and reveals and --

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.534
-Are there four children?
-There are four children.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:05.701
-Okay.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.868
-They are between
the ages of 10 and 12.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.167
They get lost.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.133
They come from
a kind of mysterious planet.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:15.000
They get blasted off and lost
in the world of "Star Wars."

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.501
And Jon Watts,
the brilliant director

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:20.200
of the last
"Spider-Man" trilogy,

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.934
he headed up the directors
and he --

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:26.100
Yeah, it's got a little more --
Well, they described it

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.667
as is a little more
Amblin, meaning,

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.701
you know, it's
an adventure of kids,

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.000
but it's not in the kids world.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.367
The jeopardy is real.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.434
-And it was a blast,
I'll tell you.

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:40.167
-What's it like being on those
giant sets of "Star Wars"?

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:43.534
-The thing I underestimated
was the experience

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:46.033
of acting opposite droids

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.634
and creatures,
which, of course, are all there.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.901
And so you get to work
with, at times, you know,

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:53.400
five, six, seven puppeteers.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.701
And these people are masters.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.267
So, you know,
your conversations are like,

00:02:58.267 --> 00:02:59.467
"Oh, who does the left arm?

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:00.734
Okay, you do the left arm.

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.100
So, do you want to put
the left arm, like, here

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.934
or when you look at me --"
And it's a really weird,

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:07.234
different type of acting,
but it's fun.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:08.601
And then, of course,
you got to pinch yourself

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:09.634
because you're sat
there surrounded

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:11.400
by this weird creature
and this --

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.567
-Yeah, yeah.
You're like, "Am I --"

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:13.901
-And then this robot.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.968
And you're doing a really
serious scene, like, talking.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.033
-It's almost like fantasy camp.
-Totally.

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:20.868
-Right? You're like, "I can't
believe I get to do this."

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.767
-I got --
I've been very lucky.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:28.801
I've worked with some
particularly respectable actors.

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:32.567
But I've never been star-struck
like I was when I met a Jawa.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:33.601
-Yeah.
-I'm not joking.

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:37.300
-Yes!
-I saw a Jawa walking by.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.934
I was like,
"Oh, I can't believe.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.834
It's real Jawa."
-"It's a real Jawa."

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.200
Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.701
-Is Jon Favreau
involved with this one?

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:44.968
-Yes, he is.
-Oh, he is.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.234
-Yeah.
-He's fantastic, man.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.567
-He is.
-I like that guy.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:50.200
-And he's got a wonderful
family feel

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.601
in Manhattan Beach,
where we shot it.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.734
There were a couple
of other projects going on.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:56.567
Yeah, it was a
really wonderful experience.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:59.868
I hope you will have
the same experience watching it.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:01.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We're excited. It'll be good.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.601
-Thank you.

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:06.200
-I want to talk about
"Peter Pan &amp; Wendy."

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.400
-Yeah.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.601
-You were almost
unrecognizable as Captain Hook.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:13.267
There you are. Yeah.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.133
-The dastardly.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:16.968
-Dastardly.
-Dastardly is right. Yeah.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.100
That's a fun call
to get, though, huh?

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.767
Again, speaking of,
like, kind of dreams,

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.534
I mean, "Star Wars," obviously,

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.267
but also "Peter Pan" and Disney.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:27.501
-Yeah. It was a little daunting.
-Yeah.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:28.701
-Filling some big boots.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.801
-Yeah, some great actors
have played --

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.400
-Really great actors.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.300
But this -- There was
a great take in this script

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.634
where you understand
a little more about

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:40.534
why Hook is the way he is,
how he came to Neverland,

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:43.868
the relationship between him and
Peter and how it really started.

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:47.200
And so you really get into,
I suppose,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.300
understanding a little bit of
the damage that was done to him

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.801
and why he's quite
as awful as he is.

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:56.501
And we went back to the book
for some detail and insight.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.834
But, obviously, you know,
I leaned pretty heavily

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:00.801
comfortably on the shoulders
of the great actors

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.200
who have played him before

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.267
and I hope brought a little bit
of my own insight, yeah.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:08.300
-I feel like it
must be, like, so much fun

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.701
to walk on a giant pirate ship
as Captain Hook.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:14.234
You'd be like, "That's right.
Yeah, respect."

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.934
-It's up there.
-"Respect."

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:19.100
-It's up there with,
yeah, as far as --

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:22.300
You realize, I suppose,
suddenly, how easy it is

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.834
for a group of men
dressed as pirates

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:27.534
to fall into the opportunity
of living that for real.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.167
-Yeah, of course.
Yeah, you jump right in.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:30.701
-Once we were all on --

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:32.601
First of all,
this ship was extraordinary.

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.567
And they would remove the stairs

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.367
so no one could get off,
because we were on a gimbal

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:38.767
so the thing could move like
you were at sea.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:41.000
And you on there --
We were on there for hours

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.467
with our bad teeth
and the shaved heads

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:45.133
and everyone -- We "arrgh!"

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:46.767
A lot of that going on.
-Yeah.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:48.567
-Sea chanties.
-Yeah.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:51.934
-And they all
fell into calling me Captain,

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:54.667
which I didn't mind, of course.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:56.501
I was like,
"You salute me all day long."

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.534
-Were the kids scared?
Were they intimidated?

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:02.033
-So, we tried -- David Lowery,
our wonderful director,

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:04.667
had the idea of really trying
to encourage them

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:06.467
not to see me
when I wasn't Hook.

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:09.767
So I just stayed as Hook
the whole time,

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:13.968
which was an opportunity just
to be really scary and mean.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.667
Sounds kind of awful.

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:17.234
But, you know, you didn't
want -- I didn't want

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.767
suddenly to be talking to
a little 6-year-old dude,

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:20.901
and then suddenly,
it's like, "Right.

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:22.634
You hate me.
I'm Hook. I'm Hook."

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:24.901
So, instead,
I just stuck as Hook.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:26.200
-Yeah.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.634
-And, yeah, a lot of the
reactions you see in the film

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:31.767
are their reactions to me
for the first time

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.934
or as the man himself, you know?

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:37.000
-Did they ever get to meet Jude?
-They met Jude at the end.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.767
And I did what every adult
should do to bribe children.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:45.033
I hired an ice-cream van
and I drove it on-site

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.334
and gave out ice cream.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:50.367
-Come on. That's a good man.
That's exactly right.

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:53.234
-Nothing like chocolate ice
cream to persuade a child,

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:54.300
and you're alright.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.467
-"I'm not that bad, really.

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.734
Yeah, I was just playing a
character, yeah."

00:06:57.734 --> 00:07:00.934
And then the hook
is on the right hand, right?

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:03.601
-Yeah. I had to learn to
fight -- sword-fight

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:04.634
with my left hand.

00:07:04.634 --> 00:07:05.934
-Wow. That's a cool skill.

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:07.501
-Well, first of all,
I had to learn to sword-fight,

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:10.100
and then it was like, "And now I
have to learn to sword-fight."

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.701
You know what was surprising
was how un...

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.167
What's the word?

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.968
I mean, just how unskilled the
left hand, my left hand, was.

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:19.868
I had to do all these little
routines every day for an hour

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:21.334
before I was allowed
to do anything, with a weight,

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:23.701
where I had to just sort of
learn to use my --

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:27.234
I was like -- I had this
awful left hand, yeah.

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:28.467
-I heard that,
like, if you try --

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:29.734
If you're right-handed,

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:31.601
try brushing your teeth
with your left hand,

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:33.334
and it's, like,
apparently mind-blowing.

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:36.300
-Once I had the hook on,
it was hard to take it off,

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.534
because it was under
all these layers

00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:39.434
and it was strapped on
and what have you.

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.200
So I milked that all day long,

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.534
because I can fight
with my left hand, but,

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:46.267
"Oh, can you pass me the..."

00:07:46.267 --> 00:07:47.701
-Smart man.

00:07:47.701 --> 00:07:50.667
-"Pass me the cup of tea."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:53.267
-Gaffigan, Gaffigan, Gaffigan,
pass me --"

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:54.901
Jim Gaffigan is in the movie.
He plays Smee.

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:57.334
-He plays Smee.
-How's Jim Gaffigan?

00:07:57.334 --> 00:07:58.701
-Well, we would sit around --

00:07:58.701 --> 00:08:00.400
I mean, he should be in
stand-up, that guy.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.033
He's so funny.

00:08:02.033 --> 00:08:03.601
-Yeah, he should
give it a shot.

00:08:03.601 --> 00:08:05.767
-He's really entertaining.
-He should give it a try.

00:08:05.767 --> 00:08:09.067
-We'd be sat there talking for
hours about everything,

00:08:09.067 --> 00:08:11.868
and he was --
He's so smart and so humorous.

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:14.100
And then we'd both kind of laugh

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.667
because we're dressed
as pirates.

00:08:15.667 --> 00:08:16.767
-Yeah. And you're talking
a serious conversation.

00:08:16.767 --> 00:08:18.167
-Sat on a boat.

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:20.734
And then I'd be like, "Shouldn't
we be doing something?

00:08:20.734 --> 00:08:22.267
We've been at this for an hour."

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:23.334
-He's the best.

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:24.501
-And it's like,
"Do you need us at all?"

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:25.734
They're like,
"No, no, you're fine.

00:08:25.734 --> 00:08:27.000
You're just in the background."
I'm like, "Great.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.267
Jim, tell me,
what do you think about the..."

00:08:28.267 --> 00:08:29.934
-Yeah, tell me another routine.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:31.200
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.501
Here's Jude Law in
"Peter Pan &amp; Wendy."

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:34.634
Take a look at this.

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:38.133
♪♪

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:40.467
-[ Groans ]
Sorry, Captain.

00:08:41.734 --> 00:08:42.834
-Mr. Smee!

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:46.033
Smee...

00:08:46.033 --> 00:08:49.434
make a note
my cabin needs a new door.

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:51.334
-A new door, yes.

00:08:51.334 --> 00:08:53.000
Uh, right.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.534
M-Might I say, captain, uh,

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:57.901
that will be your third door
this month.

00:08:57.901 --> 00:09:02.000
-And it won't be the last.
Where's my telescope?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.701
Telescope? Smee.

00:09:04.701 --> 00:09:06.167
-Telescope at hand, Captain.

00:09:08.167 --> 00:09:11.467
-Speak not to me of hands, Smee.

00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:14.567
-Huh. I see your point. Uh...

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.868
-That's what I'm
talking about there.

00:09:19.868 --> 00:09:21.734
Jude Law, everybody.

00:09:21.734 --> 00:09:25.801
"Peter Pan &amp; Wendy" is streaming
exclusively on Disney+

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:26.968
this Friday.

00:09:26.968 --> 00:09:29.033
Joshua Jackson
joins us after the break.

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:30.300
Stick around, everybody.

